+    // ---- the carry-propagating pairs, for 128-bit add and subtract ----
+    //
+    // wasm's i64.add128 / i64.sub128 need a two-instruction chain that carries
+    // a bit from the low half to the high half. POWER keeps that bit in
+    // XER[CA], which addc/adde/subfc/subfe all read or write, so THE TWO CALLS
+    // MUST STAY ADJACENT: anything emitted between them that touches CA
+    // destroys the result. BBQ emits them back to back and resolves the
+    // register aliasing that would otherwise need an intervening move before
+    // its architecture fork, which is what makes sharing ARM64's two-line
+    // sequence correct here.
+    //
