+    // POWER's X-form indexed loads and stores are base + index, with no
+    // displacement field and no scaling, which is exactly the shape Air asks
+    // for on this target: Arg::isValidScale accepts only 1 here, and
+    // Arg::isValidIndexForm allows a displacement only for Lea, which
+    // computes an address rather than accessing memory.
+    //
+    // Taking the form still matters for the add it saves. It is no longer a
+    // hard requirement, though: AirGenerate.cpp and
+    // AirAllocateRegistersAndStackAndGenerateCode.cpp both re-enable the macro
+    // scratch under isPPC64() -- r29 and r30 are isReserved, so the allocator
+    // cannot have handed either to a live Tmp -- which is what lets the
+    // Address forms fold an out-of-form displacement through
+    // memoryTempRegister instead of refusing it.
+    //
+    // RA is the base and RB the index, never the other way round: r0 in the RA
+    // field of any load or store encodes the literal zero rather than the
+    // register, which is measured in the handbook and is the whole reason
+    // extendedOffsetAddrRegister() can be r0 at all.
