+    // ---- the link register ----
+    //
+    // There is deliberately no `linkRegister` GPR constant: on PowerPC the
+    // link register is an SPR reached through mflr/mtlr, and inventing a
+    // GPRReg for it would let generic ARM64/RISCV64-shaped code compile into
+    // something that reads the wrong register. Anything that needs the
+    // return address goes through one of these instead, and the call sites
+    // in AssemblyHelpers and CCallHelpers name PPC64 explicitly.
